148.905 DUTIES OF THE BOARD.
Subdivision 1.
General.
The board shall:
(1) adopt and enforce rules for licensing psychologists and for regulating their professional conduct;
(2) adopt and enforce rules of conduct governing the practice of psychology;
(3) adopt and implement rules for examinations which shall be held at least once a year to assess applicants' knowledge and skills. The examinations may be written or oral or both, and may be administered by the board or by institutions or individuals designated by the board. Before the adoption and implementation of a new national examination, the board must consider whether the examination:
(i) demonstrates reasonable reliability and external validity;
(ii) is normed on a reasonable representative and diverse national sample; and
(iii) is intended to assess an applicant's education, training, and experience for the purpose of public protection;
